    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0858" n="776" xml:id="pg776"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 550.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 19, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I send you the enclosed slips, (one cut
                    from a French paper of yesterday, and the other cut from Galignani of this
                    morning,) the first of which announces the sailing of a first detachment of six
                    hundred men of the Belgian legion destined to Mexico, and the other the
                    contemplated conveyance to Yera Cruz of four thousand two hundred volunteers
                    enlisted in Austria. The enlistments in Europe for service in Mexico, it would
                    seem from this and other notices I have observed, are quite prompt.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d676-a1.xml" xpointer="d676-a1"/>
